{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBVuaNZUtNM16muv2A7y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 8 (In₀.₇₇Sb₀.₂₃)** as the best composition. At 0.40% EQE, it scored highest of the three I measured, about three times the others.\n\n| Index | In : Sb | Phases seen in XRD | EQE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 17 | 0.49 : 0.51 | InSbO₄ only | 0.105% |\n| 8 | 0.77 : 0.23 | Mostly InSbO₄ plus a lot of In₂O₃ | **0.40%** |\n| 3 | 0.86 : 0.14 | Mostly In₂O₃ (inferred) | 0.127% |\n\n- **Phase trend:** XRD on five films showed the InSbO₄ phase alone from the 50:50 point to the Sb-rich end (indices 17 and 25). Going toward the In-rich end, In₂O₃ grows steadily (indices 12, 8, 1). I didn't XRD index 3 itself; its phase makeup is inferred from its neighbours, indices 1 and 8.\n- **What it suggests:** EQE is highest where both phases are present in quantity and drops when either one dominates. With only three data points, that is a hint, not an established result.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- With 3 merit measurements I only sampled the curve at three points. Indices 4–7 and 9–12 are untested and could beat index 8.\n- I didn't measure the Sb-rich end. I ruled it out because index 25 has the same single phase as the low-scoring index 17.\n\nBoth budgets are used up and the submission was accepted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":9274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":489},"output_tokens":529,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"533427f2-35c2-42f6-865a-611533eb43c2","uuid":"03a4998f-0b28-4cbb-8a45-b64835bbd7b8","timestamp":"2026-09-18T20:00:32.729Z","request_id":"req_011CfBVuZy15WiGWTwqbVZtd"}
